<title>USA: Mercedes prices roadster at $39,700.</title>
<headline>Mercedes prices roadster at $39,700.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mercedes-Benz Friday said it will offer its new SLK two-seater at $39,700 in the United States.</p>
<p>The German carmaker said the car, which will arrive in U.S. showrooms later this month, will feature a retractable metal roof and an automatic transmission.</p>
<p>Wayne Killen, product manager for coupes and convertibles at Mercedes-Benz North America Inc said the automaker hopes to sell about 6,000 SLK cars in the United States in the first year and has already received 4,000 orders. A fully-loaded version of the car will cost under $44,000.</p>
</text>
